Dhanashree Agro Sprayers Ltd, an imagined company, has authorised capital of 1,00,000 equity shares of ₹10 each. During the year it:

1. bought machinery for ₹72,000 from Parineeta Engineering Works, an imagined firm, paying in fully paid equity shares issued at ₹12;
2. offered 50,000 equity shares to the public at ₹12, payable ₹3 on application, ₹5 on allotment (including the premium of ₹2) and ₹4 on the first and final call; all were applied for and allotted;
3. received all money due except the call on 400 shares held by Heer; Yasmin, holding 1,000 shares, paid the call with her allotment money (ignore interest);
4. forfeited Heer's shares and reissued all of them at ₹8 per share as fully paid.

The company keeps Calls in Arrears and Calls in Advance accounts.

(a) Pass the journal entries. [5]

(b) Prepare the balance sheet extract with the notes on Share Capital and Reserves and Surplus, as required by Schedule III Part I. [3]
